              "id": "glog-ca138526-cd08-4ebe-9568-c41866a6ea8c",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `memcpy` function in C++ is used to copy a block of memory from one location to another. This function does not check the size of the destination buffer, which can lead to buffer overflow if the source is larger than the destination. This is a common vulnerability in C++ programming that can lead to serious security issues such as code execution, denial of service, or information disclosure.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the `memcpy` function is used to copy the content of `vendor_name` into `desc->vendor_and_architecture_name`. If the size of `vendor_name` is larger than `desc->vendor_and_architecture_name`, it can cause a buffer overflow.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always ensure that the destination buffer is large enough to hold the source data. This can be done by checking the size of the source and destination before using `memcpy`. Alternatively, you can use functions that check the size of the destination buffer such as `strncpy` or `memcpy_s`.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code snippet:\n\n```cpp\nif (vendor_name.length() < sizeof(desc->vendor_and_architecture_name)) {\n    memcpy(desc->vendor_and_architecture_name, vendor_name.c_str(), vendor_name.length());\n} else {\n    // Handle error\n}\n```\n\nIn this fix, we first check if the size of `vendor_name` is less than the size of `desc->vendor_and_architecture_name`. If it is, we proceed with the `memcpy`. Otherwise, we handle the error.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `<cstring>`: This library provides the `memcpy` function.\n- `<string>`: This library provides the `std::string` class.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)"
